{"title":"2021 JMC 10 Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_18\">Problem 18</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMC_10_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 18\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/692e3bee67c91837acbdcf63862b3b3c94366f28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"32\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are positive real numbers that satisfy the equation\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/e/86e8bf90f3dcd7b5cae5bf0aaf684d9a89898df2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[xy+yz+xz=96(y+z)-x^2 = 24(x+z) -y^2 = 54(x+y) -z^2,\\]\" width=\"478\" height=\"19\" />\nwhat is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/7/d57d8fef9329fabd73078ae824a034e8a00e332f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xyz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"11\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/3/e43bebf2f4d0f9df677661a9217d72e508559b72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 1720 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 2720 \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 7560 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 9600 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 15120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"498\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMC_10_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Putting terms of different degrees on different sides, we can factor to obtain; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/e/d8e97bb77f920a0be0102645d020651172d3a136.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{cases} 96(y+z)= (x+y)(x+z)  \\\\ 24(x+z)=(y+z)(x+y) \\\\ 54(x+y)=(x+z)(y+z) \\end{cases}\\]\" width=\"221\" height=\"74\" /> Multiplying these and simplifying yields  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/5/3452ac2b3939cc7705d9faafd55d32f074c94d2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+y)(y+z)(x+z)=96 \\cdot 24 \\cdot 54,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"276\" height=\"18\" /> and substituting gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/f/35f8e34c391b73954d2da35981d13aa3596b3b8f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[96(y+z)=\\frac{96 \\cdot 24 \\cdot 54}{(y+z)} \\implies (y+z)^2=24 \\cdot 54=1296 \\implies y+z = 36.\\]\" width=\"532\" height=\"42\" /> Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/4/064147603dc5bc340eaf1199e2695e2ee0256abb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+z=72$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/2/c821d662cc2b528b7481f94a5940e9c7dff7cfb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y=48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/b/68bc0bab76847a58f18a619d04b09fc1bda63f7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y,z) = (42,6,30)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"158\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/9/7a9b1a1afaef3732a7fd48b3ca06d00e3e2ab5eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xyz=42 \\cdot 6 \\cdot 30 = 7560,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"189\" height=\"16\" /> as desired.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018015713\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.007 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.008 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 51/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2449/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:21041:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018015713 and revision id 150772. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}